    <article style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.8;">
      <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: var(--step-3, 2rem); color: var(--text-main); font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 24px;">About</h1>
      
      <p style="color: var(--text-main); font-size: 1.02rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        <strong>AlwaysNever-25</strong>, also known as <strong>Al</strong>.<br>
        Born sometime after Y2K, he's a boy with no knowledge at all regarding website.<br>
        Until he did something bold. Jumped immediately... into Wikia.
      </p>

      <p style="color: var(--text-main); font-size: 1.02rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        Well, he thought he did something, with uploading images of weapons from this old Zombie MMO game called The Last Stand: Dead Zone.<br>
        He got sidetracked by a zombie game, but time flies. He went through the standard hurdles, namely, High School and College.
      </p>

      <p style="color: var(--text-main); font-size: 1.02rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        He slept through class, yet somehow he ended up being the fourth best in his class by the end of the senior year? What?<br>
        Yeah, it is a mystery. His interest piqued again as he got to edit another wiki.<br>
        A name now forgotten. He met some cool people with wizard knowledge on HTML and CSS, and a reddit moderator. Bless <em>his</em> soul.
      </p>

      <p style="color: var(--text-main); font-size: 1.02rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        He then learned the beautiful world of HTML and CSS, and basically, front-end development. Found some kind of purpose, but he was still into this Wikia work first.<br>
        After the now forgotten Wiki was abandoned, he jumped ship into other wikis. Editing constantly.<br>
        Somehow got admin in three different wikis, even founded one of those. <del style="color: var(--text-muted); opacity: 0.6;">It would've been four if he was smart enough but he's not</del>
      </p>

      <p style="color: var(--text-main); font-size: 1.02rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        By then he was already familiar with the structure of Wikia, now branded as Fandom.<br>
        He learned how to apply CSS to the whole wiki, applying scripts from the Dev Wiki to his own, and feverishly editing a wiki that perhaps nobody even looks at.
      </p>

      <p style="color: var(--text-main); font-size: 1.02rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        And then you know what? He went to a bootcamp. After all that effort, he finally started applying those skills to a real-world equivalent, not just in his head.<br>
        Perhaps, later on, he can actually apply it to real-world projects, the things in his mind.
      </p>
